>>__ load "simpLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `add_looper`

``` hol4
simpLib.add_looper : string * (simpLib.simpset -> tactic) ->
  simpLib.simpset -> simpLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds a named looper to a simpset.

A looper is a tactic that `simpLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC` tries when
simplification and the final solvers leave a goal unsolved; the
subgoals it produces are simplified again. `add_looper (name, mk) ss`
adds the looper `mk`, which is passed the simpset in use, after the
existing loopers. A looper with the same name is replaced in place.

A looper should fail (or raise `Conv.UNCHANGED`) when it does not apply,
and make progress when it succeeds.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val ss = simpLib.add_looper ("conj", fn _ => CONJ_TAC)
     boolSimps.bool_ss;
>> simpLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false} ss [] ([], “p ∧ q”)
     (Context.snapshot());
```

